# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: MesaLibs, riscos-mesa's shared libraries.
Package: MesaLibs
Section: Library
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: SharedLibs, SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport
Recommends: RISC3D
Components: Resources.!MesaLibs (LookAt)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-mesa
Description: OpenGL, EGL, GLU, GLUT, SDL 2 and OpenAL as shared libraries
 riscos-mesa's shared libraries for "mixed" programs (such as TORCS and
 YSFlight): OSMesa (OpenGL 2.1, OpenGL ES), EGL, GLU, freeglut, SDL 2,
 OpenAL Soft and the GPU library for a Pi 4, in !Boot.Resources, so
 programs share one copy. It adds the hard-float loader (ld-riscos/so/2)
 and SOManager 3.04 to !SharedLibs where it hasn't got them. With RISC3D
 installed programs draw on the GPU; without it, in software. Restart
 after installing or upgrading it.
Build-Map: !MesaLibs -> Resources/!MesaLibs
Build-Trigger: PostInstall triggers/MesaLibs/PostInstall
Build-Notice: MesaLibs, packaged for PackMan from riscos-mesa's release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-mesa/releases
 .
 Mesa 20.3.5 and 26.1.6 (MIT), GLU (SGI Free Software Licence B 2.0),
 freeglut (MIT/X), SDL (zlib) and OpenAL Soft (GNU LGPL 2 or later;
 being a shared library, it can be replaced); SOManager and the
 hard-float loader in !MesaLibs.SharedLibs are GCCSDK's (the loader
 derives from Linux's ld.so 1.9.9, BSD-style). Licences follow.
Build-Copyright: !MesaLibs/Licences
